cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TesserACT: a de novo short-read genome assembler for bacterial isolates"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TesserACT contributors"
    alias: iowa69
repository-code: "https://github.com/iowa69/TesserACT"
abstract: >-
  TesserACT assembles haploid bacterial isolates from paired-end Illumina reads.
  It builds a de Bruijn graph over a ladder of k-mer sizes, simplifies it,
  resolves repeats with paired-end evidence, closes gaps and polishes the
  result, in C++17 with no dependencies beyond a compiler, zlib and pthreads.

  Where a repeat is longer than a sequencing fragment there is no paired
  evidence that can settle it, and TesserACT stops rather than guessing.
  Supplying a genus model, learned from closed genomes of the same organism,
  lets it settle those junctions from independent evidence instead.
keywords:
  - genome assembly
  - de Bruijn graph
  - bacterial genomics
  - short reads
  - Klebsiella pneumoniae
license: MIT
version: 1.2.4
date-released: 2026-08-03
